## 📚 Learning Objectives

* Learned git clone.
* Learned git pull.
* Learned the basic Git workflow.
* Learned how to use the style tag.
* Learned how to change fonts using CSS.

## Git Commands

### Clone Repository

```bash
git clone <repository-url>
```

Downloads a repository from GitHub.

### Pull Changes

```bash
git pull
```

Downloads the latest changes from GitHub.

## New HTML Tag

```html
<style>
</style>
```

Used to write CSS inside HTML.

## First CSS Property

```css
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}
```

Changes the font of the webpage.

## Practical Work

* Added a style block.
* Changed the font of the webpage.

## Key Takeaways

* CSS controls appearance.
* The style tag allows CSS inside HTML.
* font-family changes text style.
* git clone downloads repositories.
* git pull updates repositories.
